# F-22 LIGHTNING II (NovaLogic 1996) — the HUD, element for element out of the manual.
# Every row carries the page it comes from. Source of record: mods/f22/doc/hud.md, whose §2 inventory
# and §3 position map this file IS — one row per table line, in the diagram's reading order.
# Format: doc/render/hud-declaration.md.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE CANNOT SAY, and why it is here as a comment rather than as a silent omission
# (mods/f22/doc/hud.md §State carries the same list with its measurement):
#   THR: 85%          no throttle or thrust field is published on the bus
#   AIRFRAME: 100%    own damage is monotone state in core/FBSystemHealth, not a display block
#   SHOOT LIST line 1 a radar contact carries NO IDENTITY in this tree, by construction — the manual's
#                     `MIG-27 ALPHA 1` is exactly the thing CLAUDE.md's anti-cheat rule forbids
#   FLAPS             no flap position is published
# Four elements of twenty-one. They are not drawn empty: a row that cannot be fed is not declared.

hud f22
scale 1.75
color 0.35 1.00 0.45
inset 12
tfov 25

text x 0.5 y 0 dy 30 align c size 3 text "NO TELEMETRY" color 1.0 0.8 0.2 when !telemetry

# ---- Compass Heading Indicator: horizontal line across the TOP, periodic heading marks, the current
# heading in a box centred on it, and the waypoint steering caret ON the band — which becomes an
# off-band cue when the selected waypoint is not on the shown arc [MAN p.30, hud.md §2].
compass y 0.09 span 90 step 5 count 2 src heading src2 steer_rel_brg

# ---- Waypoint Data, three lines, upper left [MAN v]: id, the special instruction for it, range in NM.
# Line 2 is a LITERAL: a `.fbm` waypoint carries no instruction text (doc/mods.md §Gaps, briefings).
text x 0 dx 10 y 0 dy 62 size 1.15 fmt "WAYPOINT %1.0f" src steer_num
text x 0 dx 10 y 0 dy 78 size 1.15 text "FOLLOW ROUTE"
text x 0 dx 10 y 0 dy 94 size 1.15 fmt "RANGE: %5.2f" src steer_dist_nm

# ---- Airspeed Indicator, vertical line down the LEFT: knots up to Mach 1, a MACH NUMBER above it
# [MAN v]. Two declarations of one instrument, switched by the same threshold the manual names.
tape x 0.07 y 0.5 src cas_kt span 300 step 25 count 2 h 300 align l gap 0 text "KT" when !supersonic
tape x 0.07 y 0.5 src mach span 1.2 step 1 count 1 h 300 align l fmt "%4.2f" text "MACH" when supersonic

# ---- Altimeter, vertical scale down the RIGHT, feet ABOVE SEA LEVEL [MAN v].
tape x 0.93 y 0.5 src alt_ft span 4000 step 500 count 2 h 300 align r gap 0 text "FT MSL"

# ---- Pitch Ladder, centre: the tick marks on the rung tips ALWAYS POINT TO THE HORIZON [MAN v].
ladder step 5 span 45 w 150 gap 46
horizon w 300 gap 60

# ---- ASE Circle (Allowable Steering Error): kill probability is greater with the target inside it
# before firing [MAN v]. The Gunsight Pipper REPLACES it when guns are selected [MAN v].
# "WHEN GUNS ARE SELECTED" CANNOT BE DECLARED — no master mode and no selected-weapon KIND is published
# (the F-16 deck reads the same absence and works around it the same way). Two readings were measured
# and both failed: `gun_ready` (fitted, armed, loaded) is true for the whole sortie, so the ASE circle
# never appeared once; `gun_valid` (a ballistic solution exists) is true from the first radar track, and
# its lead point at 2 NM lies off the glass, so the frame had neither circle nor pipper. What IS
# declarable is gun RANGE: outside it the steering circle, inside it the sight.
circle x 0.5 y 0.5 size 90 count 32 when !gun_in_range
funnel h 44 size 8 when gun_in_range

# ---- Flight Path Indicator, a tiny dot dead centre [MAN v]. The manual calls it "where the nose is
# ACTUALLY pointing", i.e. the boresight — so it is screen-fixed and not the velocity vector.
circle x 0.5 y 0.5 size 4 count 8

# ---- Engine Management Data, four lines, lower left [MAN v]. Two of four are declarable (above).
text x 0 dx 10 y 1 dy -60 size 1.15 fmt "%+05.1FG" src g
text x 0 dx 10 y 1 dy -44 size 1.15 fmt "FUEL: %6.0f LBS" src fuel_lb

# ---- Shoot List Data, four lines, lower right [MAN v]; inactive it reads only SHOOT LIST [MAN d].
text x 1 dx -10 y 1 dy -76 align r size 1.15 text "SHOOT LIST"
text x 1 dx -10 y 1 dy -60 align r size 1.15 fmt "VC: %5.0f" src tgt_closure_kt when locked
text x 1 dx -10 y 1 dy -44 align r size 1.15 fmt "RANGE: %5.2f" src tgt_range_nm when locked

# ---- The Target Designation Box around the current target, and the Target Steering Cue that REPLACES
# it as a tiny circle when the target leaves the HUD, pointing the way back [MAN v, §4 steps 3 and 6].
contacts size 30 size2 18 len 34 gap 10

# ---- Weapon Indicators across the BOTTOM: selected weapon and rounds remaining [MAN v]. The gun's
# books sit BESIDE the rail's, not on top of them: both are true at once on this airframe.
text x 0.5 dx -14 y 1 dy -26 align r size 1.2 fmt "%2.0f" src weapon_count when station_selected
text x 0.5 dx -6 y 1 dy -26 align l size 1.2 text weapon when station_selected
text x 0.5 dx 70 y 1 dy -26 align l size 1.2 fmt "GUN %4.0f" src gun_rounds when gun_ready

# ---- Status fields, bottom strip: GEAR down, BRAKE extended, RADAR on [MAN d, MAN v].
text x 0.5 dx -60 y 1 dy -10 align c size 1.1 text "GEAR" when gear_down
text x 0.5 dx 0 y 1 dy -10 align c size 1.1 text "BRAKE" when speedbrake
text x 0.5 dx 60 y 1 dy -10 align c size 1.1 text "RADAR" when radar_on

# ---- Attack Display inset, upper right, toggled on/off [MAN v]. About 25 miles is where the manual
# starts the engagement sequence (§4 step 1), so that is the inset's range scale.
scope x 0.84 y 0.26 w 120 h 90 span 25 when radar_on

# ---- Instrument Landing System: three RED lines, two vertical and one horizontal, active ONLY within
# 6 miles of the runway and below 5 000 ft AGL [MAN p.31, hud.md §5]. Overlapped verticals plus a
# centred glideslope form the cross that is the on-profile picture.
ils x 0.5 y 0.5 w 90 h 90 span 5 color 1.0 0.25 0.25 when ils_window
